Third-party files in viewer/vendor/

This project is unofficial and is not affiliated with, or endorsed by, the Excalidraw project.
The files below are copied unmodified from npm tarballs fetched from registry.npmjs.org with
`npm pack --ignore-scripts`. Each tarball's sha512 matched the integrity value in package-lock.json
(which equals the registry's dist.integrity) before extraction. viewer/vendor/MANIFEST.sha256 lists a
SHA-256 for every vendored file, and `python3 scripts/vendor.py --check` verifies them.

1. @excalidraw/excalidraw 0.17.6, MIT licence
   Tarball integrity: sha512-fyCl+zG/Z5yhHDh5Fq2ZGmphcrALmuOdtITm8gN4d8w4ntnaopTXcTfnAAaU3VleDC6LhTkoLOTG6P5kgREiIg==
   Files:
     dist/excalidraw.production.min.js and its notices file dist/excalidraw.production.min.js.LICENSE.txt
     excalidraw-assets/ : six fonts (Assistant, Cascadia, Virgil) and the lazy-loaded chunk
       vendor-677e88ca78c86bddf13d.js with its notices file vendor-677e88ca78c86bddf13d.js.LICENSE.txt.
       The chunk holds the file-saving code (showSaveFilePicker, createWritable and the download fallback)
       and also Mermaid-to-Excalidraw, d3, DOMPurify, js-yaml and pica. Without it, "Save to..." and
       the exports do nothing. Its notices file lists the licences of the libraries bundled in it.
   Not included: the 53 locale files in excalidraw-assets/locales/ (the English interface loads without them).
   The tarball itself ships no LICENSE file; its package.json declares "MIT". The licence text in
   viewer/vendor/excalidraw/LICENSE was taken from the project's tag:
     https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/blob/v0.17.6/LICENSE
     tag v0.17.6 (annotated, 2024-04-17T19:57:47Z) -> commit 0dbd2a39319d41fda37b2945dea0dcbd58d6a564
     1,067 bytes, git blob 8a844bc750a313db95d147bea9e4c9537b2cebc0 (scripts/vendor.py checks this hash)
   The npm tarball has no provenance attestation, so nothing ties it cryptographically to that tag.

